{"name":"Beautiful Darkness","hex":"#686d70","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beautiful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Possessing beauty, impressing the eye; attractive. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Used emphatically or ironically, after the noun it qualifies."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who is beautiful. Can be used as a term of address."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beautiful"},{"term":"darkness","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being dark; lack of light; the absolute or comparative absence of light.","The state or quality of reflecting little light, of tending to a blackish or brownish color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/darkness"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beautiful Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Beautiful Darkness is a young adult paranormal romance novel written by Kami Garcia and Margaret Stohl. The second novel in the Caster Chronicles, it was published by Little, Brown on October 12, 2010."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/70/Beautiful_Darkness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beautiful_Darkness"},{"title":"Beautiful Darkness (graphic novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Beautiful Darkness is a graphic novel illustrated by French illustrators Marie Pommepuy and Sébastien Cosset under their pen name Kerascoët, and written by Pommepuy and Fabien Vehlmann. Beautiful Darkness was first published in English by Drawn & Quarterly in 2018 in a translation by Helge Dascher."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/69/Jolies_T%C3%A9n%C3%A8bres_Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beautiful_Darkness_(graphic_novel)"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence